WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.280
An evil robot babysitter, a 75-ft&nbsp;
shark, and one of Spider-man's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.540
biggest enemies! These are the sci-fi&nbsp;
films you don't wanna miss in 2023!

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:15.060
One of the most highly anticipated movies&nbsp;
of 2023 has got to be "Dune: Part Two," the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:20.460
follow-up sequel to 2021's massive adaptation&nbsp;
of Frank Herbert's science fiction magnum opus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:26.160
Both "Dune" and "Dune: Part Two" come to us from&nbsp;
critically acclaimed director Denis Villeneuve.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.720
The man who's no stranger to sci-fi, having&nbsp;
created incredible films like "Arrival" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.120
"Blade Runner: 2049." "Dune" is the story of&nbsp;
a royal family in the distant future that is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:41.640
exiled to the remote desert planet of Arrakis,&nbsp;
which is home to everything from the enigmatic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.640 --> 00:00:47.340
native Fremen, giant hostile sandworms, and a&nbsp;
precious interstellar resource called spice.

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:50.700
Because of the massive nature of&nbsp;
the story from the original book,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:55.560
Villeneuve decided to break his films into two&nbsp;
parts to do these characters justice. "Dune:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.360
Part Two" will continue where the last film left&nbsp;
off as audiences will follow Paul Atreides and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:05.400
Chani as they lead a revolution of the Fremen&nbsp;
against the planetary occupation of the evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.400 --> 00:01:10.380
House Harkonnen. The lead role of Paul Atreides&nbsp;
is played by Timothée Chalamet. The supporting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:16.560
cast of top-tier acting talent included Zendaya,&nbsp;
Rebecca Ferguson, Stellan Skarsgård, Josh Brolin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:21.780
Dave Bautista, and Oscar Isaac in the first&nbsp;
installment alone. In the upcoming sequel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:27.300
the cast has gained even more star power.&nbsp;
Joining the cast are Florence Pugh, Léa Seydoux,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:31.860
Christopher Walken, and Austin Butler hot off&nbsp;
his performance as Elvis Presley in "Elvis".

00:01:32.580 --> 00:01:37.020
Following in the footsteps of sci-fi horror&nbsp;
movies about artificial intelligence such as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.760
"Ex Machina" and "The Terminator" comes&nbsp;
Gerard Johnstone's "M3GAN." The story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.080
follows the creation of a seemingly perfect&nbsp;
robotic doll that is supposed to serve as an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.300
ideal friend for kids and even a possible&nbsp;
babysitter for parents. But soon the evil&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:55.920
android begins to take on a mind of its own.&nbsp;
The most obvious comparison for "M3GAN" is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:00.540
to the other iconic horror franchise featuring&nbsp;
an evil toy, "Child's Play." There's even been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:05.040
some online beef between the Twitter accounts&nbsp;
for both Chucky and M3GAN to hilarious effect.

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.960
"You should probably run."

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:12.360
"M3GAN" is the brainchild of Akela Cooper&nbsp;
and James Wan, the latter of which has become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.860
well-known for his work on franchise fare, such&nbsp;
as "Saw," "The Conjuring," "Fast and Furious,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:22.140
and "Aquaman." Since it's produced by Blumhouse,&nbsp;
the production company which has backed every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:27.180
Jordan Peele film to date, this movie brings back&nbsp;
Allison Williams, one of the leads of "Get Out."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:33.000
It also features the talent of Violet McGraw,&nbsp;
Ronny Chieng, Brian Jordan Alvarez, Jenna Davis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:38.400
and Amie Donald as the main characters of&nbsp;
this horror flick. Since its January release,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:44.820
M3GAN garnered a lot of attention with a viral&nbsp;
dance scene and a staggering $30 million opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:50.640
weekend at the box office. You won't want to&nbsp;
miss this strong start to 2023's sci-fi roster.

00:02:51.320 --> 00:02:56.400
Hot off the heels of their recent Holiday&nbsp;
Special, it's almost time to check back in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:01.380
with everyone's favorite team of multi-species&nbsp;
interstellar heroes in this year's "Guardians&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:06.720
of the Galaxy Vol. 3." With James Gunn back at&nbsp;
the helm of the series he created back in 2014,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.740
Marvel has allowed the Guardians to have&nbsp;
one last hurrah with the finale to their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:15.060
trilogy. Part three of the series brings back&nbsp;
all the main stars from previous appearances&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:20.100
including Chris Pratt as Starlord, Zoe&nbsp;
Saldana as Gamora, Vin Diesel as Groot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:25.860
Dave Bautista as Drax, Bradley Cooper as&nbsp;
Rocket, Karen Gillan as Nebula, and many more.

00:03:25.860 --> 00:03:29.940
Taking place in the far reaches of space&nbsp;
within the Marvel Cinematic Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:35.100
"Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3" continues where&nbsp;
the past two films left off following the ongoing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:40.320
story of this unlikely superhero team. It also&nbsp;
requires some knowledge of movies outside this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:44.280
series to fully understand what's going on,&nbsp;
since these characters were deeply affected&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:48.960
by the events of both "Avengers: Infinity War,"&nbsp;
"Avengers: Endgame," and "Thor: Love and Thunder."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:53.820
For example, the original Gamora was killed by&nbsp;
her adoptive father Thanos during the infinity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:58.560
war and was later replaced by an earlier version&nbsp;
of the character from a different timeline. Since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.940
Starlord and Gamora were developing a pretty&nbsp;
serious romance, this new dynamic will surely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.940 --> 00:04:07.860
play a part in the next installment. It's also&nbsp;
important to know how much drama there was behind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.860 --> 00:04:12.540
the scenes regarding James Gunn since he was fired&nbsp;
and, subsequently, rehired throughout production.

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:16.620
"Autobots, roll out!"

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:20.280
That's probably what at least one giant&nbsp;
shape-shifting robot will say in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.540
next edition of the massive "Transformers"&nbsp;
franchise. It seems like only yesterday that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:29.040
audiences were watching Shia LaBeouf stumble&nbsp;
around big GCI robots back in Michael Bay's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:34.560
2007 "Transformers" adaptation. Now there&nbsp;
are six mainline movies and one "Bumblebee"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:40.140
spinoff for fans to enjoy. Paramount Pictures is&nbsp;
continuing the story with 2023's "Transformers:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:44.340
Rise of the Beasts" which will function&nbsp;
as a sequel to "Bumblebee" since it takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.540
place sometime in the 1990s with all new&nbsp;
characters who've never been seen before.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.960
"Transformers: Rise of the Beasts" is directed by&nbsp;
Steven Caple Jr. It stars Anthony Ramos, Dominique&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.960 --> 00:05:00.420
Fishback, Luna Lauren Vélez, and Tobe Nwigwe are&nbsp;
the human characters who discover the transformer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.420 --> 00:05:05.520
robots on an archaeological excavation. This&nbsp;
film also features a star-studded voice cast&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:10.680
for the various Transformers both good and evil.&nbsp;
The list includes Peter Cullen as Optimus Prime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:16.440
Pete Davidson as Mirage, Sebastian Maniscalco&nbsp;
as Wheeljack, Ron Perlman as Optimus Primal,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:21.240
and Michelle Yeoh as Airazor. "Transformers:&nbsp;
Rise of the Beasts" is directly inspired by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:25.740
the "Beast Wars" era of the original toy line&nbsp;
and tie-in animated show, which establishes the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.447 --> 00:05:36.527
Everdeen and her climactic struggle against&nbsp;
the oppressive government of the Capitol.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.527 --> 00:05:40.787
Although there was a satisfying end to the&nbsp;
series for many fans, it should come as no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.787 --> 00:05:45.047
surprise that producers at Lionsgate wanted&nbsp;
to bring the franchise back to life with some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.047 --> 00:05:49.127
kind of prequel. These movies did make huge&nbsp;
amounts of money at the box office, after all!

00:05:49.127 --> 00:05:54.047
Well, that's exactly what's happening with 2023's&nbsp;
"The Hunger Games: The Ballad of Songbirds and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.047 --> 00:05:58.847
Snakes." This film is a prequel directed by&nbsp;
Francis Lawrence and based on a 2020 novel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.847 --> 00:06:04.367
by original author Suzanne Collins. It takes&nbsp;
place nearly 64 years before the events of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:08.507
original "The Hunger Games" film by focusing&nbsp;
on the early years of the Hunger Games event.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.159 --> 00:06:22.099
Lucy Gray Baird, Jason Schwartzman as Lucretius&nbsp;
Flickerman, Peter Dinklage as Casca Highbottom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.099 --> 00:06:27.199
Viola Davis as Dr. Volumnia Gaul,&nbsp;
and Hunter Schafer as Tigris Snow.

00:06:27.199 --> 00:06:29.419
"I want every camera watching."

00:06:30.139 --> 00:06:35.059
Another year, another highly anticipated Pixar&nbsp;
movie. The legendary computer animation studio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.059 --> 00:06:39.979
is back at it in 2023 with a movie that's&nbsp;
been shrouded in more mystery than their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.979 --> 00:06:44.899
usual projects. But "Elemental" got audiences&nbsp;
excited for what's to come through a recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.899 --> 00:06:49.699
trailer that revealed some information. It's&nbsp;
no secret that Pixar loves taking abstract&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.699 --> 00:06:53.299
ideas or concepts and anthropomorphizing&nbsp;
[an-thruh-puh-MOR-fai-zing] them. They did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.299 --> 00:06:58.039
this with emotions in "Inside Out" and souls&nbsp;
in "Soul," so it seems as though "Elemental"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.039 --> 00:07:01.879
is continuing that trend by portraying&nbsp;
various natural elements as people.

00:07:01.879 --> 00:07:06.859
"Elemental" takes place in Element City, a&nbsp;
metropolis where all the elements of the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:11.779
live together in harmony as conscious beings.&nbsp;
It will feature groups of little elementals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.779 --> 00:07:17.119
based on fire, water, and land as they interact&nbsp;
in an urban environment. It sounds similar to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.119 --> 00:07:22.519
Disney's 2016 film "Zootopia," but with elements&nbsp;
instead of animals. The story itself will focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.519 --> 00:07:27.079
on two elements: a fire woman named Ember&nbsp;
and a water man named Wade as they become&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.079 --> 00:07:31.579
unlikely friends despite their natural&nbsp;
differences. Its official synopsis from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.579 --> 00:07:36.199
Pixar itself goes into more detail about its&nbsp;
on-screen dynamic. The description explains,

00:07:36.199 --> 00:07:38.599
"The story introduces Ember, a tough,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.599 --> 00:07:42.139
quick-witted and fiery young woman,&nbsp;
whose friendship with a fun, sappy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.139 --> 00:07:45.979
go-with-the-flow guy named Wade challenges&nbsp;
her beliefs about the world they live in."

00:07:45.979 --> 00:07:50.119
"Elemental" is directed by Peter Sohn&nbsp;
and stars the voice acting talent of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.119 --> 00:07:54.199
Mamoudou Athie and Leah Lewis&nbsp;
as Wade and Ember respectively.

00:07:54.919 --> 00:08:00.619
As if "The Meg" wasn't big enough, it's gonna get&nbsp;
even bigger with "Meg 2: The Trench." This sequel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.619 --> 00:08:06.979
follows up on 2018's over-the-top sci-fi action&nbsp;
story about a 75-foot ancient megalodon hunting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:12.079
a group of scientists out in the Pacific Ocean.&nbsp;
This sequel continues the story of rescue diver&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.079 --> 00:08:17.839
Jonas Taylor as he must once again deal with&nbsp;
this pesky megalodon at even lower depths than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.839 --> 00:08:22.459
before. While there's little information out&nbsp;
there about the plot of "Meg 2: The Trench,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.459 --> 00:08:27.139
it's safe to assume that the plot involves both&nbsp;
another megalodon and possibly even a trench.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:33.739
"The Meg" was a surprise box office hit back&nbsp;
in 2018, making over $500 million worldwide&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.739 --> 00:08:39.619
off of a budget of only $130 million despite&nbsp;
a generally negative critical reception. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.619 --> 00:08:44.899
first film only managed to snag a 46% score on&nbsp;
Rotten Tomatoes from critics and an even lower&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.899 --> 00:08:49.759
42% score from audiences, and yet somehow&nbsp;
it did well enough to warrant a sequel.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:49.759 --> 00:08:54.379
Regarding the choice to make another "The Meg,"&nbsp;
Jason Statham himself explained the reasoning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.379 --> 00:08:58.339
during an interview with Entertainment Weekly&nbsp;
during the first movie's press tour, saying,

00:08:58.339 --> 00:09:01.399
"I think it's like anything in this&nbsp;
day and age — if it makes money,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.399 --> 00:09:05.299
there's obviously an appetite to make&nbsp;
more money. And if it doesn't do well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.299 --> 00:09:08.599
they'll soon sweep it under the carpet&nbsp;
— but that's the way Hollywood works."

00:09:09.319 --> 00:09:14.599
Yet another superhero movie on this list is DC's&nbsp;
upcoming "Blue Beetle" movie, which will bring the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:14.599 --> 00:09:19.099
iconic techy character to the big screen for the&nbsp;
first time. For those who don't know a lot about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.099 --> 00:09:23.119
the character, here's a quick crash course on&nbsp;
everything you'll need to know. Blue Beetle is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.119 --> 00:09:29.119
a superhero, whose real name is Jaime Reyes, who&nbsp;
gains powers after a blue alien scarab attaches&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.119 --> 00:09:33.919
itself to his spine. Because of this event,&nbsp;
he can form a protective exoskeleton around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:33.919 --> 00:09:39.259
his body at will which easily allows him to fight&nbsp;
crime. Basically, he's DC's answer to Spiderman.

00:09:39.259 --> 00:09:41.599
"Hi? Do I know you?"

00:09:42.259 --> 00:09:48.799
"Blue Beetle" will be directed by Angel Manuel&nbsp;
Soto and features a mainly Latino cast. The actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.799 --> 00:09:52.639
include Xolo Mariduena, Bruna Marquezine&nbsp;
[BROO-nah mark-ah-ZEE-knee], George Lopez,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.639 --> 00:09:57.739
Belissa Escobedo [beh-LIH-suh es-cuh-BAY-doh],&nbsp;
Adriana Barraza, and Damián Alcázar to name a few.

00:09:57.739 --> 00:10:02.239
In fact, this is the first film within the&nbsp;
DC Extended Universe to have a Latino lead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.239 --> 00:10:06.259
character at all, which is a big milestone&nbsp;
for the franchise. In an interview with The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.259 --> 00:10:09.919
Hollywood Reporter, Xolo Maridueña&nbsp;
discussed how essential the Latino&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.919 --> 00:10:13.999
background of the character and his family&nbsp;
was to the history of "Blue Beetle," saying,

00:10:13.999 --> 00:10:17.479
"With this character, he lives with his&nbsp;
family and there's no way to hide who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.479 --> 00:10:22.099
he is. Right from the very first moment he gets&nbsp;
his powers, his family knows. That's different."

00:10:22.699 --> 00:10:26.419
Would it surprise you to learn that even&nbsp;
more superhero movies are coming out in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:26.419 --> 00:10:30.859
2023? Of course not, there are so many&nbsp;
of them that it would be bizarre if there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.859 --> 00:10:34.819
weren't at least four per year to watch.&nbsp;
That being said, the upcoming "Kraven the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.819 --> 00:10:39.259
Hunter" adaptation differs in many ways from&nbsp;
the other sci-fi superhero flicks on this list.

00:10:39.259 --> 00:10:44.479
"Kraven the Hunter", directed by J. C. Chandor,&nbsp;
is a collaboration between Columbia Pictures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:44.479 --> 00:10:49.699
Sony, and Marvel to continue Sony's separate&nbsp;
cinematic universe of movies like "The Amazing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.699 --> 00:10:54.199
Spider-Man," "Venom," and "Morbius." It&nbsp;
will star Aaron Taylor-Johnson as the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.199 --> 00:10:59.239
larger-than-life character of Kraven the Hunter,&nbsp;
a dastardly big game hunter who has often been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.239 --> 00:11:03.919
a dangerous enemy for Spiderman throughout the&nbsp;
comics. During an interview with Comicbook.com,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.919 --> 00:11:08.599
Johnson went into detail about what kind of man&nbsp;
Kraven will be in his solo film, explaining,

00:11:08.599 --> 00:11:13.159
"This is a character that was built ages ago&nbsp;
and it's in a new time and era, but yeah,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.159 --> 00:11:16.639
is he going to be the hunter that we&nbsp;
all want to see? Yeah, absolutely."

